    rules: "Mandatory capture is absolute: a player with a jump available has no other legal move, and multi-jumps must be completed once begun. Kings are crowned on the back rank and gain backward movement and captures. A player who cannot move loses, even with pieces still on the board — blocked armies surrender. The computer plays positionally and will take every forced capture you offer, including the ones you meant as traps, so design sacrifices carefully. There is no move timer and no draw offer; games play to a finish. Your wins are tallied and saved. This is checkers as the rulebook wrote it — no house rules, no take-backs.",
